  "notes": "⚠ **`confidence` is low because the research says so outright: one strongly documented record, otherwise thin, and the entry is marked [LOW-CONF].** What that one record does establish is the construction, and that is what this model states: a pitched/chopped vocal-sample loop as the hook plus a bell layer, 4-bar loops, the key dictated by the flipped source — so `phraseBars` is weighted to 4, `harmonicRhythm` leads with `1_per_bar`, and the families are major/modal as often as minor. The INFERRED parameters are everything below the chord level: `kick.syncopation` 0.52, `hihat.fillDensity` 0.55 and the whole `bass808` block are read off \"bouncy syncopated kick\", \"straight 16th hats with rolls\" and \"short punchy 808 doubling the sample's bass\" — four prose fragments, no figures. ⚠ Authored on the 95–105 straight feel with the clap on 2 and 4; the ~140–150 half-time alternative the research also names is not modelled. ⚠ `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.5 with `answer_lick` on top is the \"plus a bell layer\" line: it is a second written part answering the sample, not an octave doubling of it. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
